@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# GOAL — block 25: the ordered phase of the three-dimensional formation law — Toom-type stability of the level automaton re-proved with an explicit noise threshold; at least six invariant laws at strong coupling (2026-09-16)
+
+**Owner directive (2026-09-16):** sync main, read the latest PRs, point at the highest-leverage science, do it. Read: the owner's drafts #8159–#8166 (the fixed-coupling compact U(1) bridge, his live personal campaign) and his closed seam blocks #8114 (glued groups) and #8122 (possibility covariance). Working the photon bridge in parallel would collide with live work; the campaign's last open record-dynamics obligation, S6 of block 12 (PR #8146), is held by nobody and is proof-shaped. Taken.
+
+**Why this block.** Block 12 shows the three-dimensional monotone formation law, read level by level, is a three-predecessor majority automaton with one-sided noise `ε(p, q, r) = max(q, r)/p + O(p^{−2})`, and reduces the ordered phase to one obligation: for small `ε`, starting from the all-`0` level, `sup_x P(η_x = 1) < 1/2`. The classical route (Toom 1980; Berman–Simon 1988; Gács 2021; Swart–Szabó–Toninelli 2022 — reference only) is a Peierls argument over "explanation trees" whose size is linear in the number of noise sites. This block re-proves it at scope for this automaton, in `Z³` level time, with every constant explicit, and closes S6: the formation reading has an ordered phase in three dimensions.
+
+**Object.** Space-time `= Z³` with level `τ(x) = x_1 + x_2 + x_3`; predecessors `x − e_i`; the noisy majority `η_x = maj(η_{x−e_1}, η_{x−e_2}, η_{x−e_3}) ∨ ζ_x`, `ζ` i.i.d. Bernoulli(`ε`), `η ≡ 0` at levels `≤ 0`; noise sites `= {ζ_x = 1, fewer than two 1-predecessors}`; the graph `G` on `Z³` with arrows (`x — x − e_i`) and forks (`x — x ± (e_i − e_j)`), degree `12`; the functionals `M_k(z) = z_k − τ(z)/3`, `Σ_k M_k ≡ 0`, with `M_k(x − e_j) − M_k(x) = 1/3 − δ_{jk}`.
+
+**Contract.**
+- T1 (clusters and the cause graph): clusters at a level = components of the arrow graph on `1`-sites through levels `≤` that level; a noise site is a singleton cluster; the cause graph of a cluster (its predecessor clusters, joined by forks) is connected.
+- T2 (spanned sets): `Span(P, v_1, v_2, v_3) = Σ_k M_k(v_k)`, `Size(P) = Σ_k max_P M_k`; the excuse lemma: for a non-noise `1`-site `v` with winning pair `W(v)`, `Excuse_k(v) := argmax_{W(v)} M_k` satisfies `Σ_k M_k(Excuse_k(v_k)) = Span + 1`; a fork pair has `Size = 1`.
+- T3 (the spanning lemma): for a spanned set `(L, u)` and a family of subsets connected by intersection covering the poles, there are spanned subsets with the same total span whose reduced point sets form a minimal connecting system — with the full proof (the partition of charges at each point).
+- T4 (the explanation tree): the refinement operation (delete the cluster, keep the poles that carry edges, add the tree of child clusters and forks, add one arrow per kept pole) preserves the tree property, raises the span by at least one, adds at most three arrows; termination; the final tree has `n` noise nodes, `n − 1` forks (contract the arrows) and at most `4(n − 1)` edges.
+- T5 (counting): rooted subtrees of `G` with `k` edges and `0/1` marks number at most `2^{k+1}(4·12)^k`.
+- T6 (the Peierls bound): `P(η_x = 1) ≤ Σ_{n≥1} ε^n Σ_{k ≤ 4(n−1)} 2^{k+1} 48^k ≤ (192/95) ε/(1 − 96⁴ ε)`; for `ε ≤ ε_0 := 1/(2·96⁴)`, `sup_x P(η_x = 1) ≤ (384/95) ε < 1/2`.
+- T7 (the formation law): with block 12's domination (re-proved), `P(v_x ≠ a) ≤ (384/95) ε(p, q, r)` from the all-`a` level whenever `ε(p, q, r) ≤ ε_0`; `ε` is strictly decreasing in `p`; at `(p, 1, 2)` this holds for `p ≥ p_0` (exact, computed); Cesàro limits give six invariant laws of the level automaton, pairwise distinct: the ordered phase; block 08's uniqueness region and this region are disjoint.
+- Executed: the whole construction on every noise configuration of the depth-2 backward cone (1024), every depth-3 configuration with at most four noise sites, random deeper cones and structured seeds — the tree property, the marks, the spanning identity at every refinement, and `edges ≤ 4(n − 1)`; the subtree counts for `k ≤ 3` against `48^k`; the Peierls arithmetic and `p_0` exactly.
+
+**Lens pass (self-run panel).**
+- *"This is Toom's theorem."* Yes; re-proved at scope for this automaton with explicit constants, in the campaign's currency (the last open row of record dynamics), and with the construction executed exhaustively on small cones — which is more than the literature's expositions offer.
+- *"The threshold is absurd (`ε_0 ≈ 6·10^{−9}`, `p_0 ≈ 10^{8}`)."* Known weakness of the route (the published crude bounds are `3^{−21}` and `1/(32·24^8)`); the theorem is the existence of the ordered phase with an explicit region, not its location.
+- *"Fork–fork adjacency."* The control's first draft let two forks sharing a point be adjacent in the cause graph, skipping the cluster between them and losing a noise node; the tree must alternate clusters and forks (the bipartite cause graph). Fixed before the contract.
+- *"Six laws or six extremal laws?"* Six distinct invariant laws are proved outright; the extremal count uses the extremal decomposition, named at definition level.
+
+**Forbidden phrases (beyond the lane's standing list):** "phase transition", "critical", "converge", "certified", "emergent", "Toom's theorem is derived" (the theorem is classical; it is re-proved).
+
+**Prior-art search at `origin/main` (6dda46fc1a).** Nothing on Toom contours, eroders or space-time Peierls arguments; block 12 (open PR) states the obligation; blocks 08–11 (open PRs) define the formation law; block 01 (main) the rule.
+
+**Sharpening (2026-09-16, after the PR opened).** Contract addendum: replace T5's depth-first count by the lift of the explanation trees to the typed regular tree, with the marks read off the tree (a node is marked iff it has no arrow to a predecessor; at most one such arrow per node), the arrows and forks weighted separately under `forks = n − 1`, `arrows ≤ 3(n − 1)`, and the weight sum bounded by an exact rational super-solution of the three-term recursion; target `ε_0 = 7/10⁶`, bound `3/10⁵`. Lens: *"You cannot assume the arrows point down."* Correct — the control refuted that candidate lemma (`538` of `4308` trees reach a kept pole from below); the count keeps both directions. *"Is the lift injective?"* Yes: the projection recovers the tree from the words. *"Is the super-solution argument exact?"* Yes: the truncated sums are increasing polynomials bounded by induction; the three inequalities are rational arithmetic. Forbidden phrase added for this addendum: "convergence" (write: the edge of the recursion's domain).
