 Stacked on #8002 → #8000 → #7999 → #7998 → main; all hand-offs. Block 05 = the monotone-order class: one formation law for every linear extension of the product order (every rule); rows and columns path chains; the 2×2 corner law with corner independence; no right/down turning staircase is first-order Markov in its site values (proved for every nonconstant positive orbit triple under the declared product-rule monotone law); opposite corner classes give the same finite-rectangle law, with two distinct laws only at the executed 2×3 triples; the snake keeps rows and can lose column chains (column 0 survives on 3×3; on the executed 4×3 no column is a chain). Lens before the primary caught the supervisor's own wrong snake control. Historical checker: FIX FIRST on one forbidden mechanism sentence (false; deleted), nothing refuted in the theorems. Lock released.
 
 Current source review found five further P2 groups, corrected in the canonical note and runner with their disposition in REVIEW_HISTORY.md. Same-session confirmation is pending; this appendix records an open review handoff.
+
+## 2026-09-16 block 25 opened for review as PR #8168 (supervisor)
+Independent PR against `main` (`6dda46fc1a`); parent on `main`: block 01. The owner's directive (sync main, read the latest PRs, take the highest-leverage science): his drafts #8159–#8166 are his live personal campaign on the fixed-coupling compact U(1) bridge, and his closed seam blocks #8114/#8122 cover glued groups and possibility covariance; block 12's obligation S6 was held by nobody. Block 25 = the stability of the noisy level automaton re-proved at scope: clusters and the connected cause graph (T1); the excuse identity along `M_k = z_k − τ/3` (T2); the spanning lemma with the bipartite cluster–fork tree (T3); the refinement whose span rises by `≥ 1` per step and equals the fork count at the end, giving `edges ≤ 4(n − 1)` (T4); marked subtrees `≤ 2·96^k` (T5); `P(η_x = 1) ≤ (192/95)ε/(1 − 96⁴ε) ≤ 1/42024960` for `ε ≤ 1/(2·96⁴)` (T6); with block 12's domination re-proved, the formation law from a constant plane stays within `1/42024960` of it at every site and has six invariant laws whenever `ε(p,q,r) ≤ ε_0`, at `(p,1,2)` for `p ≥ 339738628` (T7). Runner 22 checks, 13 mutations in-family, exact, seconds; the construction executed exhaustively on the depth-2 cone and all depth-3 configurations with `≤ 4` noise sites. Refuting pass: abstract spanning-lemma instances, float enumeration, an independent graph implementation, direct summation, simulation (stable to `ε = 0.05`, collapse at `0.08`) — the one finding (fork–fork adjacency) caught and fixed by the control before the contract. Gates: pipeline ×2, changed-evidence, `audit_lint --strict`, `git diff --check`, vocabulary lint clean on the block's files. Next: the queue refresh at block 25 opening (sharpen the threshold; the intermediate band; the normalization; X4).
+
+## 2026-09-16 block 25 sharpened on the open PR #8168 (supervisor)
+Same branch and PR, same seat protocol (control → contract addendum with a lens pass → primary → refuting pass → fold → census → gates). T5's depth-first count (`2·96^k`, `ε_0 = 1/(2·96⁴)`) replaced by the lift to the typed regular tree of the twelve edge types with the marks read off the tree, at most one arrow to a predecessor per node, and separate arrow/fork weights under `forks = n − 1`, `arrows ≤ 3(n − 1)`; an exact rational super-solution of the recursion at `(91/1000, 1000/107653)` gives `Σ_T t^a s^f < 391/100`, hence `P(η_x = 1) ≤ (391/100)ε ≤ 3/10⁵` for `ε ≤ 7/10⁶` and `p_0 = 285718` at `(p, 1, 2)` (was `339738628`; factor `1189`). A candidate lemma on the way — every arrow points away from the root — was refuted by the executed trees (`538` of `4308`) and dropped. Runner still 22 checks / 13 mutations (`certificate_wrong` replaces `series_constant_wrong`), cache re-pinned; the refuter iterated the recursion in floats (divergence at `1.06 s`), ran the crude binomial split as a second bound (`44` times weaker), recounted the upward arrows independently and simulated at `ε_0` (density `8.3·10^{−6}` against `3·10^{−5}`). Remaining slack of the route: the arrow budget (`12/7` observed against `3`) and the union bound; the edge of the recursion's domain is near `7.4·10^{−6}`. Gates re-run; PR body updated. Next: the queue refresh below.
+
+## 2026-09-16 value gate after block 25's sharpening (supervisor)
+The queue's next item (the arrow budget) was probed before being taken: `743` explanation trees on random cones of depth `8`–`12` include one with `7/3` arrows per fork, so `arrows ≤ 2(n − 1)` is false for the construction and the item is dropped (gain below a factor two). The remaining items — the band between block 08's uniqueness region and block 25's ordered region (the true transition, near `ε ≈ 0.05` by simulation, i.e. `p ≈ 40·max(q, r)`, against a proved `p ≥ 285718`), the kernel's normalization on `Z³`, value-dependent order laws beyond the plaquette (X4) — are hard with no route in hand; the owner's lanes (light/clock/gauge, the compact U(1) bridge, #8159–#8167) and record-matter are held. The lane's proof-shaped items are exhausted at this date; blocks 12–25 are open PRs #8146–#8158 and #8168 awaiting the owner's review loop.
