+# RESULTS — block 25: the three-dimensional formation law has an ordered phase — stability of the noisy level automaton with an explicit threshold, six invariant laws (2026-09-16)
+
+**Deliverables (branch `physics-loop/admissibility-induced-law-block25-formation-law-ordered-phase-toom-stability-level-automaton-20260916`, independent PR against `main` at `6dda46fc1a`; parent on `main`: block 01):** the note `docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THREE_DIMENSIONAL_FORMATION_LAW_ORDERED_PHASE_STABILITY_OF_THE_NOISY_LEVEL_AUTOMATON_EXPLICIT_THRESHOLD_SIX_INVARIANT_LAWS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-16.md`; the runner `scripts/admissibility_rule_three_dimensional_formation_law_ordered_phase_stability_noisy_level_automaton_2026_09_16.py` (22 checks, 13 mutations, exact, two seconds; the explanation-tree construction embedded and executed exhaustively on small cones; the tree count against the generating-function recursion); the pinned cache; the controls (`specs/supervisor_control_block25_toom_core.py` — the construction — `specs/supervisor_control_block25_toom_stability.py`, and `specs/supervisor_control_block25_sharpening.py` for the sharpened count) and the refuting passes (`specs/supervisor_control_block25_refuter.py`, `specs/supervisor_control_block25_sharpening_refuter.py`) with outputs; `GOAL_block25.md`; `CHECKER_block25_findings.md`; this record. Blocks 06–24 remain open as PRs #8034, #8035, #8138–#8142, #8146–#8158.
+
+**Why this block.** The owner asked (2026-09-16) to sync main, read the latest PRs and take the highest-leverage science. His drafts #8159–#8166 are his live personal campaign on the fixed-coupling compact U(1) bridge; the campaign's last open record-dynamics obligation — block 12's S6, the stability of the noisy majority eroder that decides whether the formation reading orders in three dimensions — was held by nobody and is proof-shaped.
+
+## Result, in one paragraph
+In level time the three-dimensional formation law is a three-predecessor majority automaton with one-sided noise `ε(p,q,r) = max(d_1, d_2, d_3)`, strictly decreasing in `p`, dominating the coarse-graining "not `a`" (T0, re-proved). A one at `x` that is not itself a noise site has a winning pair of one-predecessors; following excuses along the three charges `M_k(z) = z_k − τ(z)/3` (each rising by `1/3` along a suitable predecessor; their sum is zero) and joining pieces at one level by forks between siblings, the refinement of spanned clusters — the cause graph of a cluster is connected (T1); the excuse identity `Σ_k M_k(Excuse_k(v_k)) = Span + 1` and fork pairs have size one (T2); the spanning lemma redistributes a span over a minimal cluster–fork tree without changing its total (T3) — produces a tree of arrows and forks through one-sites rooted at `x` whose span rises by at least one per refinement and equals the fork count at the end, so that with `n` noise nodes it has exactly `n − 1` forks and at most `3(n − 1)` arrows, every node has at most one arrow to a predecessor and the noise nodes are exactly the nodes with none (T4). Such trees lift injectively to admissible subtrees of the typed regular tree of the twelve edge types, whose weight sum with `t` per arrow and `s` per fork obeys a three-term recursion bounded by an exact rational super-solution: at `(t, s) = (91/1000, 1000/107653)` it is below `391/100` (T5), so `P(η_x = 1) ≤ (391/100)ε ≤ 3/10⁵` uniformly in `x` for every `ε ≤ ε_0 = 7/10⁶` (T6). Hence, whenever `ε(p, q, r) ≤ ε_0` — at `(p, 1, 2)` for `p ≥ 285718` — the formation law started from a constant plane keeps every later site within `3/10⁵` of that value, and its level automaton has at least six distinct translation-invariant invariant laws: an ordered phase (T7). The construction is executed on every noise configuration of the depth-2 backward cone, on every depth-3 configuration with at most four noise sites, on random cones of depth `3`–`10` and on line and triangle seeds: the tree property, the marks, the spanning identity at every refinement and the edge bound hold in every case (largest ratio `2.875`); the `66103` subtrees with at most four edges are counted against the recursion's coefficients.
+
+**Sharpened after opening (2026-09-16).** The first count (a depth-first word with a mark per node: `2·96^k` trees with `k` edges, `ε_0 = 1/(2·96⁴) = 1/169869312`, `p_0 = 339738628` at `(p, 1, 2)`) was replaced by the lift to the typed tree with the marks read off the tree; the threshold rose by a factor `1189` and `p_0` fell to `285718`. A candidate lemma on the way (every arrow points away from the root) was refuted by the executed trees and dropped; the count keeps both arrow directions. The exploration puts the edge of the recursion's domain near `7.4·10^{−6}` for this accounting, so the route's remaining slack is in the arrow budget `3(n − 1)` (the executed trees never exceed `12/7` arrows per fork) and in the union bound, not in the count. At `ε = 7·10^{−6}` a `300×300` simulation gives a density of ones `8.3·10^{−6}` against the bound `3·10^{−5}`.
+
+## Certificate
+- Runner: `TOTAL: PASS=22 FAIL=0`; 13 mutations each in its family (`certificate_wrong` replaces the first count's `series_constant_wrong`; `subtree_bound_wrong` now removes an up-slot from the recursion); no floating-point literal or conversion; authors' names only in the allowed sections.
+- Refuting pass (`CHECKER_block25_findings.md`): the spanning lemma on 169 random abstract cluster–fork systems with an independent implementation; the noise map against direct floating-point enumeration at 200 random real weights; the tree checks with an independent graph implementation on 363 explained random cones; the series constant by direct summation; the automaton simulated on a periodic `96×96` level plane — stable up to `ε = 0.05` and collapsing at `0.08` (a physics sanity check; the rigorous threshold is `7·10^{−6}`). Sharpening refuter: the recursion iterated in floating point (fixed point below the certificate; divergence at `1.06 s`); the crude binomial-split bound as a second valid route (threshold `1.6·10^{−7}`, the recursion wins by `44`); the Peierls partial sum over the `64490` enumerated family trees at `ε_0` (`6.6·10^{−7}`, below `ε_0 R̄`); an independent recount of the upward arrows (`32` of `3253` exhaustive trees); the simulation at `ε_0`. One finding before the contract, folded: the first draft of the construction let two forks sharing a point be adjacent in the cause graph, skipping the cluster between them; the very first depth-2 configuration then had more edges than `4(n − 1)`; the bipartite cause graph fixed it.
+- Claim type `bounded_theorem`; status `bounded-support`; trace `upstream_support`; audit required.
+
+## Not claimed
+The location of the true threshold (the route's constant is `7·10^{−6}`; simulation puts the automaton's threshold near `0.05`); the formation law's phase between block 08's uniqueness region and this one; other menus or orders; any reading, rule or coupling as physical.
